 ## Unique Capabilities
 
-| Command | Use it for |
-|---|---|
-| `lists add` | Persist fetched candidates and personal notes |
-| `lists compare` | Compare saved facts offline |
-| `lists refresh` | Fetch current details and report changes |
-| `lists alternatives` | Match saved backups against explicit constraints |
-| `lists audit` | Find unfetched, unknown or old evidence |
+These capabilities aren't available in any other tool for this API.
 
-For saved-candidate planning, read [docs/saved-lists.md](docs/saved-lists.md).
+### Offline decisions
+- **`lists compare`** — Compare saved restaurants, meal budgets and personal notes without network requests.
+
+  _Use this when choosing between candidates already saved for the trip._
+
+  ```bash
+  tabelog-pp-cli lists compare tokyo-bars --agent
+  ```
+- **`lists alternatives`** — Find saved substitutes matching a candidate's verified area, category and optional meal budget.
+
+  _Use this when choosing a backup from the saved set using specific known facts._
+
+  ```bash
+  tabelog-pp-cli lists alternatives tokyo-bars --for 13005012 --match area,category --meal dinner --budget-max 5000 --agent
+  ```
+
+### Freshness and evidence
+- **`lists refresh`** — Update selected saved restaurants and see changed facts while keeping personal notes.
+
+  _Use this when a saved candidate needs current facts before a meal decision._
+
+  ```bash
+  tabelog-pp-cli lists refresh tokyo-bars 13005012 --agent
+  ```
+- **`lists audit`** — See which saved candidates have unfetched, unknown or old facts before requesting more details.
+
+  _Use this to select the exact saved candidates that need further checking._
+
+  ```bash
+  tabelog-pp-cli lists audit tokyo-bars --require hours,payment,reservation,dinner_budget --max-age 24h --agent
+  ```
+
+### Trip notes
+- **`lists add`** — Keep fetched restaurants and personal notes in a named trip list that can be resumed offline.
+
+  _Use this after fetching a candidate that should remain in the trip shortlist._
+
+  ```bash
+  tabelog-pp-cli lists add tokyo-bars 13005012 --note "Ginza bar option" --agent
+  ```
 
 ## Accuracy and boundaries
 
@@ -64,3 +99,51 @@
 - Distinguish source-unknown facts from details not fetched. Report bounded coverage, stale data and partial refresh failures. `--data-source local` makes zero source requests; a cache miss does not mean no restaurants exist.
 - On failure, inspect stdout for usable partial results and stderr for diagnostics. Domain errors are JSON under `--agent`; global flag-parser errors can be text.
 - Booking, payment/account changes, live availability/open-now conclusions, walking routes and bulk review/image harvesting are outside this CLI's scope.
+
+## Recipes
+
+### Keep a discovery response compact
+
+```bash
+tabelog-pp-cli find --area tokyo --cuisine bar --meal dinner --budget-max 5000 --limit 5 --agent --select items.id,items.name,items.rating,items.url
+```
+
+Project candidate identity, rating and links while retaining essential provenance and coverage metadata.
+
+### Compare saved candidates offline
+
+```bash
+tabelog-pp-cli lists compare tokyo-bars --agent
+```
+
+View saved facts and notes together; separate meal budgets and unknowns remain visible.
+
+### Refresh one saved candidate
+
+```bash
+tabelog-pp-cli lists refresh tokyo-bars 13005012 --agent
+```
+
+Fetch current detail facts for this ID, report changes and preserve its note and last valid snapshot on failure.
+
+### Find a factual saved backup
+
+```bash
+tabelog-pp-cli lists alternatives tokyo-bars --for 13005012 --match area,category --meal dinner --budget-max 5000 --agent
+```
+
+Match only within the saved set using verified area/category and a known cached dinner-bracket upper bound.
+
+### Audit evidence before more fetching
+
+```bash
+tabelog-pp-cli lists audit tokyo-bars --require hours,payment,reservation,dinner_budget --max-age 24h --agent
+```
+
+Distinguish details not fetched, source-unknown values and old snapshots without network calls.
+
+## Auth Setup
+
+The verified public English Tabelog sources require no account or API key. Optional MCP uses stdio and starts only when explicitly invoked.
+
+Run `tabelog-pp-cli doctor` to verify setup.
